## Conclusions
The temperature dependence and hysteresis of stepped sorption isotherms associated with structural transitions was studied for three flexible MOFs: Fe(bdp) with \(\mathrm{CH}_{4}\) , \(\mathrm{Co}(\mathrm{bdp})\) with \(\mathrm{CH}_{4}\) , and ZIF-7 with \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) . A five-parameter model developed to describe sorped sorption isotherms enabled the transition pressures, \(p_{\mathrm{tr}},\) widths, \(\sigma_{:}\) , and hysteresis \(\delta p_{\mathrm{tr}}\equiv\left(\frac{p_{\mathrm{tr}}^{(\mathrm{ads})}-p_{\mathrm{tr}}^{(\mathrm{des})}}{p_{\mathrm{tr}}^{(\mathrm{des})}}\right)\) , to be consistently and robustly analyzed. In contrast to capillary condensation, \(\delta p_{\mathrm{tr}}\) increases with temperature with a Clausius–Clapeyron dependence. At low temperatures, \(\delta p_{\mathrm{tr}}\) approaches an asymptotic limit proportional to \(p_{\mathrm{tr}}^{(\mathrm{des})}\) . The MOFs' structural phase transitions are entropically driven with enthalpy changes ranging from 5 to \(3\,\mathrm{kJ}\) \(\mathrm{mol}^{-1}\) . Curiously, the structural transition enthalpy for \(\mathrm{CH}_{4}\) on \(\mathrm{Co}(\mathrm{bdp})\) is \(60\%\) larger in adsorption than desorption, possibly due to multiple effects occurring simultaneously or asymmetrically along the two isotherm branches.
## Methods
Gas adsorption measurements. A volumetric measurement system (model ASAP2020 by Micromeritics) was used to measure ZIF-7 sorption capacity for \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) along multiple isotherms31. Before the isotherm measurements, the ZIF-7 sample27 was thoroughly dehydrated and degassed by heating stepwise to \(473\,\mathrm{K}\) under high vacuum overnight. The degassed sample was cooled to room temperature and backfilled with helium. Adsorption isotherms for \(\mathrm{CO}_{2}\) on ZIF-7 were measured in the temperature range of \(233{-}293\,\mathrm{K}\) at pressures up to \(120\,\mathrm{kPa}\) . The adsorption temperatures were controlled by a homemade heating jacket connected to a thermostatic liquid bath (Ultra-Low Refrigerated Circulators JULABO FP88) filled with either silicone oil (for \(T\!>\!283\,\mathrm{K}\) ) or ethanol \(\langle T\leq283\,\mathrm{K}\rangle\) . The temperature of the bath fluid was measured by a \(100\,\Omega\) platinum resistance thermometer.
The equilibration required at each pressure was determined automatically by the ASAP2020 system with the criterion being a relative pressure change of \(<\!0.01\%\) over an interval of \(15\,\mathrm{s}\) . For the adsorption measurements on ZIF-7, the equilibration time varied from \(5\,\mathrm{min}\) to \(15\,\mathrm{h}\) across all temperatures, with an average value of \(92\,\mathrm{min}\) . For the desorption measurements, the equilibration time ranged from \(5\,\mathrm{min}\) to \({\sim}4\) days, with an average value of \(2\,\mathrm{{h}}\) . The longest equilibration times occurred at low temperatures (233 and \(238\,\mathrm{K}\) ) and pressures less than \({\sim}1\,\mathrm{kPa}\) . The relative combined standard uncertainty of sorption capacity, \(u_{\mathrm{c}}(q_{\mathrm{i}})/q_{\mathrm{i}}\) , measured with this ASAP2020 was estimated previously31,32 to be \(1.4\%\) .
